    </header>

    <section class="summary">
      Product engineer with 8+ years across backend/product engineering, customer-facing technical delivery, and startup
      operations. I have led enterprise partner deployments, built integration tooling and developer docs,
      productionized messy business-critical data, and recently shipped two AI-assisted products end-to-end as a solo
      builder. Not a career FDE yet, but strong adjacent experience: working directly with stakeholders, connecting
      systems, translating business problems into shipped software, and communicating clearly across engineering,
      product, finance, ops, and customers.
    </section>

    <div class="layout">
      <section>
        <h2>Experience</h2>

        <article class="item experience-item experience-separator">
          <h3>Senior Product Engineer <span class="company">· <a href="https://topi.eu">topi.eu</a></span></h3>
          <div class="meta">Jul 2023 – Jun 2025 · Germany (remote)</div>
          <div class="context">Hardware subscription fintech — CoolBlue, Cyberport & MediaMarkt across Europe.</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Led end-to-end technical deployment for a <a href="https://financefwd.com/de/macquarie-topi/">€50M+
                enterprise financing partner</a>, owning stakeholder communication across Finance, Risk, Ops, Product,
              and Engineering from initial scoping through integration and production rollout.</li>
            <li>Designed, architected, and shipped <a
                href="https://developer.topi.eu/docs/topi-elements/what-is-topi-elements">topi Elements</a> — a
              partner-facing UI integration library that reduced retailer integration time by 20%.</li>
            <li>Created the <a href="https://developer.topi.eu/">topi Developer Docs</a> in 2 weeks, giving enterprise
              retail partners and sales teams a clear technical integration path.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="item experience-item">
          <h3>Senior Software Engineer <span class="company">· <a href="https://shopify.com">Shopify</a></span></h3>
          <div class="meta">Feb 2022 – May 2023 · Germany (remote)</div>
          <div class="context">Retail engineering org — scaling Shopify POS from 20 to <a
              href="https://changelog.shopify.com/posts/shopify-scales-to-1-000-locations">1,000 physical locations</a>.
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Shipped Shopify POS features across React/Rails in a fast-paced retail engineering environment,
              supporting scale from 20 to <a
                href="https://changelog.shopify.com/posts/shopify-scales-to-1-000-locations">1,000 physical retail
                locations</a>.</li>
            <li>Managed complex pricing changes for POS Pro subscriptions, coordinating product, engineering, UX, and
              business stakeholders.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <aside class="quote experience-separator">
          <p>"Nick is technically strong, a fast learner and takes initiative to solve problems. He is a team player and
            a great communicator and will be a great value to any team."</p>
          <cite>— Justin Yek, VP Finance, Airwallex (was Nick's direct manager)</cite>
        </aside>

        <article class="item experience-item">
          <h3>Support Solutions Engineering, Team Lead <span class="company">· <a
                href="https://smartly.io">Smartly.io</a></span></h3>
          <div class="meta">Jun 2018 – Jan 2022 · Singapore + Germany</div>
          <div class="context">Ad-tech unicorn. Joined as employee #203; grew through hyper-growth to 600+ employees.
          </div>
          <ul>
            <li>Acted as a bridge between customers, support, product, and engineering, translating operational pain
              into internal tools and product feedback.</li>
            <li>Led Support Solutions engineers across EMEA/APAC, mentoring a team of 7 and improving technical support
              delivery.</li>
            <li>Built internal automation with Jira, Python Airflow, and APIs, reducing manual coordination work.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <aside class="quote experience-separator">
          <p>"I've personally seen him rock it as a writer, as a team lead, as a software engineer, as a project
            manager, as a mentor, and as a brilliant coworker."</p>
          <cite>— Milan Rudez, Product Manager, Smartly.io (was Nick's teammate, then direct report)</cite>
        </aside>

        <article class="item experience-item">
          <h3>Web Development Instructor <span class="company">· <a href="https://generalassemb.ly">General
                Assembly</a></span></h3>
          <div class="meta">Dec 2016 – May 2018 · Singapore</div>
          <div class="context">Pioneer in global tech bootcamps. This is where my tech career began.</div>
          <ul>
            <li>3 cohorts, 45 students, 100% graduation rate; 30 graduates placed as engineers or PMs.</li>
            <li>Published a <a href="https://nickang.com/2017-03-12-general-assembly-singapore-review/">bootcamp
                review</a> that led to ~60 inbound messages from prospective students globally.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <aside class="quote experience-separator">
          <p>"Nick is patient, logical, and approaches every single challenge with a zealous attitude."</p>
          <cite>— Zhao Loong Ng, Software Engineer, GovTech Singapore (was Nick's student)</cite>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <aside>
        <section class="side-section">
          <h2>Founder Track</h2>

          <article class="item founder-note">
            <h3>Founder</h3>
            <div class="meta">2025 – present · Remote</div>
            <div class="context">Left employment to build software products from zero to live users, solo.</div>
            <ul>
              <li><strong><a href="https://nickang.com/album/">album.so</a></strong> — private family photo-sharing app.
                Built production web/iOS system end-to-end with auth, media uploads, storage limits, video processing,
                push notifications, and AI-assisted development workflow.</li>
              <li><strong><a href="https://nickang.com/youtionary/">youtionary.com</a></strong> — AI language-learning
                app using OpenAI APIs, Gemini real-time voice, personalized learning memory, Supabase, mobile/web
                delivery, and automated review generation. Built and deployed solo.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

        </section>

        <section class="side-section">
          <h2>Stack & Capabilities</h2>
          <div class="skills">
            <span class="pill">Backend/API integration</span>
            <span class="pill">AI agents & LLM APIs</span>
            <span class="pill">React/Node/TypeScript</span>
            <span class="pill">Ruby on Rails</span>
            <span class="pill">Python</span>
